      en: "Oldebroek is an extensive municipality in the northern part of Gelderland, featuring a captivating blend of agricultural polders and the dense forests of the Veluwe. The municipality possesses deep-seated agrarian roots, still clearly visible today in the structure of numerous traditional farmsteads and wide-open pastoral landscapes. A key cultural landmark is the 'De Bovenstreek' Farm Museum, which provides visitors with a detailed look into the historic rural lifestyle of the region. Geographically, Oldebroek borders the Veluwemeer, granting the area additional tourist appeal for water sports. Historically, the region has long been associated with military activities, maintained today through the Oldebroekse Heide, a major artillery firing range. The municipality comprises several villages, with Oldebroek and Wezep serving as the primary residential hubs. Despite ongoing modernization, the community has successfully retained its rural character and strong social cohesion. For nature lovers, the surrounding area offers a variety of hiking and cycling paths through the diverse landscape of heathlands and woods.",
